# f1 = spoil, f2 = run: a fact ends in a callee that is said to write nothing: the value of a field, in a loop.
# THE LIE lays the row of the call of `spoil` false: it writes no field of an object. By that row nothing in the loop writes what `o.held` reads, so the read stands in front of the loop, and the program says 1 where it should say 2.
# Where proofs are checked at run time (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, which --aot-harden=proof-checks stands for) the process must end by name. It did not, IN A LOOP: what is remembered was asked only where an operation had built
# nothing but constants, and a read carried out has built a record; and the test whether the slot is filled, built for its check in the turn, was itself carried in front of the loop by the row that it audits: the check in the
# turn hung on a test from in front of the head. Now the test of a check is built where it stands, and an answer that comes from in front of the loop is read again in the turn and compared.
# Under the lie alone the second line is `1,1,1,1,1,1,` and the process ends with 0 (no RUN of its own: the lane that lays the word on every RUN would stop it by name).
# RUN(NAMED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining testing=RowSaysLess:Callee/f1/ObjectFields,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# NAMED: 1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,
# NAMED-NEXT: AOT: f2 at {{*}}: what memory holds where the compiler remembers another value is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it. It is: another value or a test that once passed fails. This is a bug in Bun.
# NAMED-NEXT: crashed with
# RUN(INTURN): walk f2 mechanisms=all-Inlining testing=RowSaysLess:Callee/f1/ObjectFields,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# INTURN: = GetSlot {{*}} key="held"
# INTURN: isLoopHead=true
# INTURN: [[filled]]: boolean @Boolean = IsSlotFilled {{*}} key="held"
# INTURN-NEXT: CheckProof [[filled]] checkedType=true {{*}}source=Field
# INTURN: = GetSlot {{*}} key="held"
# INTURN: CheckProof {{*}} checkedType=true {{*}}source=WhatIsRemembered
# INTURN: = CallDirect {{*}}function=f1
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
